# =============================================================================
# WHITELIST MODE — everything is ignored unless explicitly re-allowed below.
#
# Why: this repo is the PUBLIC RELEASE SUBSET (docs + code), not the project
# folder. The project folder also holds things that must never reach a public
# remote: Meshtastic channel configs (private PSKs), power logs (timestamped
# occupancy patterns), the Layer-0 inventory (what you own and where it is),
# personal PDFs, and terabytes of models/corpora. With a whitelist, a careless
# `git add .` physically cannot leak them — the default answer is NO.
#
# To track something new, add a `!` line for it. Think before you do.
# =============================================================================

# Ignore every top-level entry...
/*

# ...then re-allow exactly the public subset:
!/.gitignore
!/LICENSE
!/README.md
!/00_DOCS/
!/05_SCRIPTS/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Junk and runtime artifacts, ignored even inside the whitelisted folders.
# (Order matters: these come AFTER the `!` rules so they win.)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/

# Script runtime output (regenerated constantly; logs can reveal patterns)
power_log.csv
latest.json
oracle.log
checksums.csv
agent_transcript*.jsonl
agent_scratch/

# Editors / OS noise
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.tmp

# =============================================================================
# NEVER whitelist these (they are already ignored by /* — this is a reminder):
#   00_INVENTORY/   — bin locations + serials of everything you own
#   01_MODELS/      — terabytes
#   02_CORPORA/     — terabytes + personal PDFs
#   03_SOFTWARE/    — installers, mirrors
#   04_CONFIG/      — meshtastic/ contains PRIVATE CHANNEL KEYS
#   06_MONUMENT/    — excluded from backups and from hope
# =============================================================================
